Description: The stereo layer's per-file 3D input menu for pictures and videos, kept in the shared store (ORDER 512 and 551)
 The context menu's "3D Input Format" is Stereo::FileChoiceMenu of the shared stereo layer: Automatic, Not 3D, every
 packing in either order, the anaglyph pairs, picture and depth, Swap left and right eyes, Save the correction into the
 file. The choice is kept in the layer's per-file store and never in the file; the swap (Alt+Shift+W) moves there and no
 longer writes a file attribute. Videos get the menu with a video's list. A file's choice follows it when it is renamed
 or moved (Stereo::FileChoiceMoves). Needs libstereo-layer-dev (>= 1.18.0).
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-14
